// Title: Lazarus "Operation Dream Job" - Smart App Control Tampering
// Description: After escalating to SYSTEM via CVE-2026-68820 (Windows AFD.sys
//   privilege escalation), Lazarus deploys the FudModule 3.1 kernel-mode
//   rootkit, which disables Windows Smart App Control by forcing its
//   VerifiedAndReputablePolicyState value to 0. This is a high-fidelity,
//   rarely-legitimate registry change - Smart App Control state is not
//   normally toggled by user or admin action once enabled, and disabling it
//   via direct registry write (rather than the OS setting UI) is a strong
//   defense-evasion indicator.
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1068 (Exploitation for Privilege Escalation), T1014
//   (Rootkit), T1562.001 (Impair Defenses: Disable or Modify Tools)
// Data source: Microsoft Defender for Endpoint (DeviceRegistryEvents)
// False positives: Very low. Legitimate Smart App Control state changes
//   happen through Windows Security settings (WSCore/related processes),
//   not raw registry writes from arbitrary processes - inspect
//   InitiatingProcessFileName for anything other than expected OS
//   components before treating as benign.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where ActionType == "RegistryValueSet"
| where RegistryKey has @"CI\Policy"
| where RegistryValueName =~ "VerifiedAndReputablePolicyState"
| where RegistryValueData in ("0", "0x0", "%%0")
| project Timestamp, DeviceName, ActionType, RegistryKey, RegistryValueName, RegistryValueData,
    InitiatingProcessFileName, InitiatingProcessFolderPath, InitiatingProcessCommandLine,
    InitiatingProcessSHA256, InitiatingProcessIntegrityLevel, InitiatingProcessAccountName
| order by Timestamp desc
